IMPORT `wra3-pt4-s77-84`

-- wra3-pt4-s85-90.l4: the Welfare Reform Act 2012 (United Kingdom), 2012 c. 5, Part 4, sections 85 to 90
-- (care homes, hospital in-patients, prisoners, claims and awards, the report to Parliament, abolition of disability living
-- allowance). Part wra3, layer 1. Written from inputs/ukpga-2012-5.txt, a plain-text rendering of legislation.gov.uk
-- (version 2026-07-01), not the official text.
--
-- A result named "is not barred as payable" means only that this provision's bar does not apply on these facts; it never
-- means the amount is payable. JUST FALSE is the text's own "no"; NOTHING is "not covered". Sections 85(1) and 86(1) are
-- powers to make regulations: the Act states the condition (85(2), 86(2)) and leaves the bar itself to the regulations, so
-- whether the regulations so provide is an input (NOTHING when unknown).

§ `s 85 Care home residents`

-- (3) "care home" means an establishment that provides accommodation together with nursing or personal care.
-- src:1450 | (3) In this section “care home” means an establishment that provides accommodation together with nursing or personal care.
@ref s 85(3) (src:1450)
GIVEN `the establishment provides accommodation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the establishment provides nursing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the establishment provides personal care` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 85(3) the establishment is a care home` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the establishment provides accommodation` AND (`the establishment provides nursing` OR `the establishment provides personal care`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“care home” means an establishment that provides accommodation together with nursing or personal care" (a closed definition)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- (4) The services that are "qualifying services": accommodation, board, personal care, and such other services as may be prescribed.
-- src:1451 | (4) The following are “qualifying services“ for the purposes of subsection (2)—
-- src:1452 | (a) accommodation;
-- src:1453 | (b) board;
-- src:1454 | (c) personal care;
-- src:1455 | (d) such other services as may be prescribed.
@ref s 85(4) (src:1451-1455)
DECLARE `s 85(4) service` IS ONE OF
    `s 85(4)(a) accommodation`
    `s 85(4)(b) board`
    `s 85(4)(c) personal care`
    `s 85(4) another service`

@ref s 85(4) (src:1451-1455)
GIVEN `the service` IS A `s 85(4) service`
      `regulations prescribe the other service for the purposes of section 85(4)(d)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 85(4) the service is a qualifying service` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the service`
    WHEN `s 85(4)(a) accommodation` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 85(4)(b) board` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 85(4)(c) personal care` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 85(4) another service` THEN
        CONSIDER `regulations prescribe the other service for the purposes of section 85(4)(d)`
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "The following are “qualifying services”" does not say that nothing else is one, and the other services are left to regulations
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the services that may be prescribed are not among the sources
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- (5) the "specified enactment" is an enactment specified by regulations for the purposes of subsection (2), or of a
-- description so specified.
-- src:1456 | (5) The reference in subsection (2) to a “specified enactment” is to an enactment which is specified for the purposes of that subsection by regulations or is of a description so specified.
@ref s 85(5) (src:1456)
GIVEN `regulations specify the enactment, or a description it falls within, for the purposes of section 85(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 85(5) the enactment is a specified enactment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `regulations specify the enactment, or a description it falls within, for the purposes of section 85(2)`
    WHEN JUST TRUE  THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The reference ... to a “specified enactment” is to an enactment which is specified for the purposes of that subsection by regulations or is of a description so specified"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the regulations are not among the sources
    WHEN NOTHING    THEN NOTHING

-- (7) "enactment" includes an enactment in an Act of the Scottish Parliament, or in an instrument made under one.
-- src:1458 | (7) In this section “enactment” includes an enactment comprised in an Act of the Scottish Parliament or in an instrument made under such an Act.
@ref s 85(7) (src:1458)
DECLARE `s 85(7) provision` IS ONE OF
    `s 85(7) an enactment comprised in an Act of the Scottish Parliament`
    `s 85(7) an enactment comprised in an instrument made under an Act of the Scottish Parliament`
    `s 85(7) any other provision`

@ref s 85(7) (src:1458)
GIVEN `the provision` IS A `s 85(7) provision`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 85(7) the provision is an enactment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the provision`
    WHEN `s 85(7) an enactment comprised in an Act of the Scottish Parliament` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 85(7) an enactment comprised in an instrument made under an Act of the Scottish Parliament` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“enactment” includes" the two named kinds; the text does not say what else is or is not one
    WHEN `s 85(7) any other provision` THEN NOTHING

-- (2) The condition: the person is a resident of a care home in circumstances in which any of the costs of any qualifying
-- services provided for the person are borne out of public or local funds by virtue of a specified enactment.
-- src:1449 | (2) The condition is that the person is a resident of a care home in circumstances in which any of the costs of any qualifying services provided for the person are borne out of public or local funds by virtue of a specified enactment.
@ref s 85(2) (src:1449)
GIVEN `the person is a resident of a care home` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `any of the costs of any qualifying services provided for the person are borne out of public or local funds` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the costs are borne by virtue of a specified enactment` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 85(2) the person meets the condition` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The condition is that the person is a resident of a care home in circumstances in which any of the costs ... are borne out of public or local funds by virtue of a specified enactment" (a limb fails)
    `s 78(6) the conjunction of the results` (LIST `the person is a resident of a care home`, JUST `any of the costs of any qualifying services provided for the person are borne out of public or local funds`, `the costs are borne by virtue of a specified enactment`)

-- (1) Regulations may provide that no amount of personal independence payment attributable to entitlement to the daily
-- living component is payable for a period when the person meets the condition in (2).
-- src:1448 | (1) Regulations may provide that no amount in respect of personal independence payment which is attributable to entitlement to the daily living component is payable in respect of a person for a period when the person meets the condition in subsection (2).
@ref s 85(1) (src:1448)
GIVEN `the person meets the condition in section 85(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `regulations provide that no amount attributable to the daily living component is payable for a period when the person meets the condition` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 85(1) the amount attributable to the daily living component is not barred as payable` MEANS
    CONSIDER `regulations provide that no amount attributable to the daily living component is payable for a period when the person meets the condition`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        CONSIDER `the person meets the condition in section 85(2)`
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no amount in respect of personal independence payment which is attributable to entitlement to the daily living component is payable in respect of a person for a period when the person meets the condition in subsection (2)" (and the regulations so provide)
        WHEN JUST TRUE  THEN JUST FALSE
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): whether the person meets the condition has not been determined
        WHEN NOTHING    THEN NOTHING
    -- the regulations do not so provide, so this bar does not apply
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        CONSIDER `the person meets the condition in section 85(2)`
        -- the bar is for "a period when the person meets the condition", so it cannot apply to a person who does not
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether regulations so provide is not among the sources
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `s 86 Hospital in-patients`

-- (3) whether any of the costs are borne out of public funds is "to be determined in accordance with the regulations".
-- src:1464 | (3) For the purposes of subsection (2) the question of whether any of the costs of medical or other treatment, accommodation and related services provided for a person are borne out of public funds is to be determined in accordance with the regulations.
@ref s 86(3) (src:1464)
GIVEN `the determination made in accordance with the regulations` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 86(3) whether any of the costs are borne out of public funds, as determined in accordance with the regulations` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the determination made in accordance with the regulations`
    WHEN JUST b  THEN JUST b
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the question "is to be determined in accordance with the regulations", which are not among the sources
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- (2) The condition: the person is undergoing medical or other treatment as an in-patient at a hospital or similar
-- institution in circumstances in which any of the costs of the treatment, accommodation and any related services provided
-- for the person are borne out of public funds.
-- src:1463 | (2) The condition is that the person is undergoing medical or other treatment as an in-patient at a hospital or similar institution in circumstances in which any of the costs of the treatment, accommodation and any related services provided for the person are borne out of public funds.
@ref s 86(2) (src:1463)
GIVEN `the person is undergoing medical or other treatment as an in-patient at a hospital or similar institution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any of the costs of the treatment, accommodation and any related services provided for the person are borne out of public funds` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 86(2) the person meets the condition` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The condition is that the person is undergoing medical or other treatment as an in-patient at a hospital or similar institution in circumstances in which any of the costs ... are borne out of public funds" (a limb fails)
    `s 78(6) the conjunction of the results` (LIST (JUST `the person is undergoing medical or other treatment as an in-patient at a hospital or similar institution`), `any of the costs of the treatment, accommodation and any related services provided for the person are borne out of public funds`)

-- (1)(a) and (b): regulations may provide, for either or both components, that no amount attributable to that component is
-- payable for a period when the person meets the condition in (2).
-- src:1460 | (1) Regulations may provide as mentioned in either or both of the following paragraphs—
-- src:1461 | (a) that no amount in respect of personal independence payment which is attributable to entitlement to the daily living component is payable in respect of a person for a period when the person meets the condition in subsection (2);
-- src:1462 | (b) that no amount in respect of personal independence payment which is attributable to entitlement to the mobility component is payable in respect of a person for a period when the person meets the condition in subsection (2).
@ref s 86(1) (src:1460-1462)
GIVEN `the component` IS A `Component of personal independence payment`
      `the person meets the condition in section 86(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `regulations provide that no amount attributable to the daily living component is payable for a period when the person meets the condition` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `regulations provide that no amount attributable to the mobility component is payable for a period when the person meets the condition` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 86(1) the amount attributable to the component is not barred as payable` MEANS
    CONSIDER (CONSIDER `the component`
              WHEN `daily living component` THEN `regulations provide that no amount attributable to the daily living component is payable for a period when the person meets the condition`
              WHEN `mobility component`     THEN `regulations provide that no amount attributable to the mobility component is payable for a period when the person meets the condition`)
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        CONSIDER `the person meets the condition in section 86(2)`
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no amount in respect of personal independence payment which is attributable to entitlement to the component is payable in respect of a person for a period when the person meets the condition in subsection (2)" (and the regulations so provide)
        WHEN JUST TRUE  THEN JUST FALSE
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): whether the person meets the condition has not been determined
        WHEN NOTHING    THEN NOTHING
    -- the regulations do not so provide for this component, so this bar does not apply
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        CONSIDER `the person meets the condition in section 86(2)`
        -- the bar is for "a period when the person meets the condition", so it cannot apply to a person who does not
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether regulations so provide is not among the sources
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `s 87 Prisoners and detainees`

-- src:1466 | Except to the extent that regulations provide otherwise, no amount in respect of personal independence payment is payable in respect of a person for a period during which the person is undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody.
@ref s 87 (src:1466)
GIVEN `the person is undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody` IS A BOOLEAN
      `regulations provide otherwise, to the extent that covers the person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 87 the amount is not barred as payable by imprisonment or detention` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person is undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE CONSIDER `regulations provide otherwise, to the extent that covers the person`
         -- the exception lifts the bar: "Except to the extent that regulations provide otherwise"
         WHEN JUST TRUE  THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no amount in respect of personal independence payment is payable in respect of a person for a period during which the person is undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody"
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
         -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether regulations provide otherwise is not among the sources
         WHEN NOTHING    THEN NOTHING

§ `s 88 Claims, awards and information`

-- (1) not entitled for any period before the date on which a claim is made or treated as made, by the person or on the
-- person's behalf. Tested a day at a time: the first day of the period against the date of the claim.
-- src:1469 | (1) A person is not entitled to personal independence payment for any period before the date on which a claim for it is made or treated as made by that person or on that person's behalf.
@ref s 88(1) (src:1469)
GIVEN `the first day of the period` IS A DATE
      `the date on which a claim for personal independence payment is made or treated as made by the person or on the person's behalf` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 88(1) the person is not barred for a period by its beginning before the claim` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the first day of the period` AT LEAST `the date on which a claim for personal independence payment is made or treated as made by the person or on the person's behalf`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is not entitled to personal independence payment for any period before the date on which a claim for it is made or treated as made"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- (2) An award is to be for a fixed term except where the person making the award considers a fixed term award would be inappropriate.
-- src:1470 | (2) An award of personal independence payment is to be for a fixed term except where the person making the award considers that a fixed term award would be inappropriate.
@ref s 88(2) (src:1470)
GIVEN `the person making the award considers that a fixed term award would be inappropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 88(2) the award is required to be for a fixed term` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person making the award considers that a fixed term award would be inappropriate` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An award ... is to be for a fixed term except where the person making the award considers that a fixed term award would be inappropriate"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- (3) In deciding whether a fixed term award would be inappropriate, that person must have regard to guidance issued by the
-- Secretary of State. The text states the duty and no consequence of failing it.
-- src:1471 | (3) In deciding whether a fixed term award would be inappropriate, that person must have regard to guidance issued by the Secretary of State.
@ref s 88(3) (src:1471)
GIVEN `the person deciding had regard to guidance issued by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 88(3) the duty to have regard to the Secretary of State's guidance is discharged` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person deciding had regard to guidance issued by the Secretary of State` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says the person "must have regard" and says nothing about what follows if they do not
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- (4) Information supplied under this Part is to be taken for all purposes to be information relating to social security.
-- src:1472 | (4) Information supplied under this Part is to be taken for all purposes to be information relating to social security.
@ref s 88(4) (src:1472)
GIVEN `the information was supplied under Part 4` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 88(4) the information is information relating to social security` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the information was supplied under Part 4` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the deeming is for "Information supplied under this Part"; the text is silent on other information
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `s 89 Report to Parliament`

-- The Secretary of State must lay an independent report on the operation of assessments under section 80 before
-- Parliament (a) within 2 years beginning with the date on which the first regulations under that section come into
-- force, and (b) within 4 years beginning with that date. The duty is the Secretary of State's, owed to Parliament; no
-- seat is built on it and no individual is a party to it.
-- src:1474 | The Secretary of State must lay before Parliament an independent report on the operation of assessments under section 80—
-- src:1475 | (a) within 2 years beginning with the date on which the first regulations under that section come into force; and
-- src:1476 | (b) within 4 years beginning with that date.
@ref s 89 (src:1474-1476)
GIVEN `the date on which the first regulations under section 80 come into force` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 89(a) the last day of the 2 years beginning with the date the first regulations come into force` MEANS
    `s 81(3) the last day of the months beginning with the day` `the date on which the first regulations under section 80 come into force` 24

@ref s 89(b) (src:1476)
GIVEN `the date on which the first regulations under section 80 come into force` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 89(b) the last day of the 4 years beginning with the date the first regulations come into force` MEANS
    `s 81(3) the last day of the months beginning with the day` `the date on which the first regulations under section 80 come into force` 48

@ref s 89(a) (src:1475)
GIVEN `the date on which the first regulations under section 80 come into force` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the report is laid before Parliament` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 89(a) the report was laid within the 2 years` MEANS
    `the date on which the report is laid before Parliament` AT MOST `s 89(a) the last day of the 2 years beginning with the date the first regulations come into force` `the date on which the first regulations under section 80 come into force`

@ref s 89(b) (src:1476)
GIVEN `the date on which the first regulations under section 80 come into force` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the report is laid before Parliament` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 89(b) the report was laid within the 4 years` MEANS
    `the date on which the report is laid before Parliament` AT MOST `s 89(b) the last day of the 4 years beginning with the date the first regulations come into force` `the date on which the first regulations under section 80 come into force`

DECLARE `s 89 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 89 lay before Parliament an independent report on the operation of assessments under section 80`

-- The duty as a regulative rule. The time is a number of days from the first day, so a #TRACE at AT 0 puts the first day at 0.
-- The deadline is the number of days from the first day to the last day of the period: an act on that day is in time.
@ref s 89 (src:1474-1476)
GIVEN `the date on which the first regulations under section 80 come into force` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Authority `s 89 act`
`s 89 the duty to lay the report within the period` MEANS
    PARTY `the Secretary of State`
    MUST `s 89 lay before Parliament an independent report on the operation of assessments under section 80`
    WITHIN (Day `the last day of the period`) MINUS (Day `the date on which the first regulations under section 80 come into force`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Secretary of State` BECAUSE "the report was not laid before Parliament within the period"

§ `s 90 Abolition of disability living allowance`

-- Sections 71 to 76 of the Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (disability living allowance) are repealed.
-- The section names disability living allowance only, so it says nothing about any other benefit.
-- src:1479 | Sections 71 to 76 of the Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (disability living allowance) are repealed.
@ref s 90 (src:1479)
GIVEN `the benefit` IS A Benefit
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 90 the benefit is abolished by the repeal of sections 71 to 76 of the Contributions and Benefits Act` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the benefit`
    WHEN `disability living allowance` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the section repeals the provisions on disability living allowance and says nothing about any other benefit
    OTHERWISE NOTHING
